{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Let there be a rakia in the midst of the waters.</b> The heavens that were created on the first day were to be spread out to be in the middle of the thickness of the waters that were over the face of all the earth, and this section is attached above. And the proof is from what is written: ״ביום עשות HaShem Elohim ארץ ושמים״ — on one day they were created; and so it explains: ״וכבר אמר Elohim יהי רקיע״ (and Elohim had already said 'let there be a rakia')." "<b>And it was dividing.</b> That the rakia would raise itself from the moment it is placed within the waters, so as to be air between it and the earth. Another interpretation: ״יהי רקיע״ — the heavens were created on the first day, as it says ״בראשית ברא Elohim את השמים ואת הארץ״. And which rakia did He create on the second day? You would say: that which is above the heads of the creatures, as it says: ״ודמות על ראשי החיה רקיע״ etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The quotation 'ביום עשות ה׳ אלקים ארץ ושמים' is from Gen 2:4b; the second quotation 'וכבר אמר אלקים יהי רקיע' is not a direct verse citation but Chizkuni's paraphrastic reference back to Gen 1:6 itself."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:18:51.214365954Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}